{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.PieriPhotonShift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.PieriPhotonShift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.pieri_self_in_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.pieri_self_in_shift","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pieri-photon-shift.lean#L72-L76","doc":"The source partition `λ` is always reachable (identity term in `γ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.pieri_one_box_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.pieri_one_box_shift","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pieri-photon-shift.lean#L60-L70","doc":"**The support-containment theorem.**\nRe-export of the `IsPieriShift` field. Intended use: callers\nquantify over `[IsPieriShift P]` and obtain the support\ncontainment for free. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:pieri-photon-shift","label":"prop:pieri-photon-shift","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pieri-photon-shift.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.IsPieriShift.support_subset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.IsPieriShift.support_subset","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pieri-photon-shift.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The shifted support lies in the one-box neighbourhood. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.IsPieriShift.support_after","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.IsPieriShift.support_after","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pieri-photon-shift.lean#L56-L56","doc":"For a degree-one Hecke element `γ` and a `λ`-block state `β`,\nthe support of `γ · β` is contained in `oneBoxShift λ`. The\n`support_after` field encodes precisely that containment as a\nfunction of the source partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.IsPieriShift.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.IsPieriShift.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pieri-photon-shift.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.IsPieriShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.IsPieriShift","kind":"class","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pieri-photon-shift.lean#L45-L58","doc":"**Pieri rule (axiomatised).**\nA degree-one Hecke element acting on a single-block state shifts\nits non-commutative Fourier support into the one-box neighbourhood.\n\nConcrete instances populate `support_after` by Pieri's rule\n[`fulton1997`, Ch. 2]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.PieriInterface.shift_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.PieriInterface.shift_self","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pieri-photon-shift.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The shift relation is reflexive: `λ ∈ oneBoxShift λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.PieriInterface.oneBoxShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.PieriInterface.oneBoxShift","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pieri-photon-shift.lean#L41-L41","doc":"The set of partitions reachable from `λ` by adding or removing\na single box. By convention `λ` itself is in this set\n(for the identity term in `γ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.PieriInterface.spectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.PieriInterface.spectrum","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pieri-photon-shift.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Spectrum (e.g. `λ ⊢ n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.PieriInterface.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.PieriInterface.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pieri-photon-shift.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.PieriInterface","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.PieriInterface","kind":"structure","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pieri-photon-shift.lean#L31-L43","doc":"Abstract data for a \"non-commutative Fourier transform\" with an\naddable/removable-corner adjacency relation on the spectrum. We\nuse this in lieu of a full partition-lattice instance, which is\nnot yet available in Mathlib. ","signatureChunk":0}]}